{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794258779,"nonce":"O8VSUVpn5qwgJ3EIP9YmuPZ/ZJI=","title":"The mesh pipeline keeps its window-sized targets after the last mesh draw","message":"From the allocation audit (code read; growth not observed in a running app).\n\nblinc_gpu mesh_pipeline.rs allocates depth, HDR, OIT accum/reveal and another target at window size (about 29 bytes per pixel, roughly 120 MB at 2560x1600), a 16 MB shadow map and the environment cubemap. `mesh_pipeline` is never set back to `None`, so they are held for the life of the app after the last mesh draw. Same class as the overlay targets (cbd7e15): free them when no frame has drawn a mesh for a while (`GpuRenderer::next_frame` / `release_idle_memory`).\n\nAlso a correctness risk: the mesh and GpuImage caches are keyed by a raw `Arc` pointer without holding the `Arc`, so a reused address can draw stale buffers.","files":null}]}